From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] debian: build Mesa 26.3.0 with the 26.2.4-1ubuntu1 packaging

Mesa 26.3.0 deleted the anti-lag Vulkan layer (moved into radv), so it is no
longer requested; lp2143073.patch (max_texture_upload_memory_budget default)
is part of 26.3.0; wayland-protocols >= 1.49 is required. The new radv
01-radv-performance.conf goes to mesa-vulkan-drivers with the other radv
defaults; the new amdgpu_list_devices developer tool is not packaged
(debian/not-installed).

